{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-05 alias policy approved (2026-08-18): every accepted alias supports both `rebar <alias> --help`/`-h` and `rebar help <alias>` without executing the handler. Exact spelling aliases reuse canonical package-data help. Compatibility shims with a distinct historical invocation (`bridge-fsck`, `bridge-probe`, `jira-onboard`) retain alias-specific package-data help that names the canonical replacement; this preserves the pinned `jira-onboard` usage spelling and existing bridge compatibility guidance. Hidden aliases such as `bridge-status` resolve explicit canonical help but remain absent from overview/completion/discovery. Retired spellings such as `purge-bridge` have neither route nor help and remain unknown. Alias metadata and retirement are validated centrally."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787068592731010001,"uuid":"300f6acb-6f19-4612-80c5-6c13d447f595"}